<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin with the reflection operator <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,y)=f(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,y)=f(y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Although <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> initially depends only on the auxiliary
coordinate <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, reflection gives <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{U}f)(x,y)=f(2x-y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{U}f)(x,y)=f(2x-y)</annotation></semantics></math>, which generally depends on both coordinates. Its macroscopic and microscopic
components are <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. The following
probabilistic representation identifies the squared norm of the microscopic
component created by reflection with an expected conditional variance, thereby
enabling quantitative estimate by the conditional Poincaré estimates used in
Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Concretely, under <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, write</p>
<table id="A2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}\coloneqq X+\sqrt{\eta}\,Z\,,\hskip 20.00003ptY_{-}\coloneqq X-\sqrt{\eta}\,Z\,,\hskip 20.00003ptZ\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)\,,\hskip 20.00003ptX\sim\mu\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}\coloneqq X+\sqrt{\eta}\,Z\,,\hskip 20.00003ptY_{-}\coloneqq X-\sqrt{\eta}\,Z\,,\hskip 20.00003ptZ\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)\,,\hskip 20.00003ptX\sim\mu\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The pair <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y_{+},Y_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y_{+},Y_{-})</annotation></semantics></math> is exchangeable. We henceforth identify
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> and write <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(y)</annotation></semantics></math> for a
macroscopic observable. Under this identification,</p>
<table id="A2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f)(y)=\mathbb{E}[f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\mathbb{E}\Var(f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f)(y)=\mathbb{E}[f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\mathbb{E}\Var(f(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To quantify the microscopic component <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f</annotation></semantics></math> created when reflection
acts on <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})^{1/2}\hskip 10.00002pt\text{on }\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>on </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})^{1/2}\hskip 10.00002pt\text{on }\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">By (<a href="#A2.E5" title="Equation B.5 ‣ B.1 Operator framework and micro–macro decomposition ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>),
<math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence</p>
<table id="A2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f\|\,,\hskip 10.00002ptf\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f\|\,,\hskip 10.00002ptf\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Thus a lower bound for <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> quantifies how much of a macroscopic
observable reflection transfers into the microscopic subspace.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Uniform macroscopic coercivity)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and set</span></p>
<table id="A2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\rm mac}\coloneqq\frac{1-\alpha\eta}{1+\alpha\eta}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\gamma_{\rm gap}\coloneqq\sqrt{1-\rho_{\rm mac}^{2}}=\frac{2\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}{1+\alpha\eta}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>mac</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>mac</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\rm mac}\coloneqq\frac{1-\alpha\eta}{1+\alpha\eta}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\gamma_{\rm gap}\coloneqq\sqrt{1-\rho_{\rm mac}^{2}}=\frac{2\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}{1+\alpha\eta}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Note that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\rm gap}\geq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\alpha\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\rm gap}\geq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\alpha\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the following hold.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(1) For every <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\in H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\in H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="4\eta\,\|\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\leq\|f\|^{2}-\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝖴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝖴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝖴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\eta\,\|\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\leq\|f\|^{2}-\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}=\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(2) Consider the mean-zero macroscopic subspace <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\coloneqq\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\cap L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\coloneqq\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P}}\cap L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\|\leq\rho_{\rm mac}\hskip 10.00002pt\text{and}\hskip 10.00002pt\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\succeq-\frac{1}{2}\,I\hskip 20.00003pt\text{on }\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>mac</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">on </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\|\leq\rho_{\rm mac}\hskip 10.00002pt\text{and}\hskip 10.00002pt\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\succeq-\frac{1}{2}\,I\hskip 20.00003pt\text{on }\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}=(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})^{1/2}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I\hskip 20.00003pt\text{on }\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">on </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}=(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})^{1/2}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I\hskip 20.00003pt\text{on }\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We prove <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> in
Appendix <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>. The identity
(<a href="#A2.E9" title="Equation B.9 ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a>) expresses <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of the
conditional variance of <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(Y_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(Y_{-})</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. Differentiating the
corresponding conditional expectation shows that this variance controls how
quickly <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f</annotation></semantics></math> changes with <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. The Poincaré inequality for
<math id="A2.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> then bounds the norm of a centered <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of
<math id="A2.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f\|</annotation></semantics></math>, giving the stated estimate.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is boundedly invertible on <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>,
(<a href="#A2.E11" title="Equation B.11 ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.11</span></a>) gives the polar decomposition</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\,:\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\longrightarrow\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\,:\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\longrightarrow\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> measures the size of the microscopic component created by
reflection, while the isometry <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> records its direction in
<math id="A2.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The next proposition says that the half-turn acts nearly as <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-I</annotation></semantics></math> on the
corresponding microscopic directions <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Global half-turn bound)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist universal constants <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c,C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c,C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that, if
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq c</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\bigr\|^{2}\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003ptv\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\bigr\|^{2}\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003ptv\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We prove <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> in
<a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sections</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> and <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Together, <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemmas</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>
provide the estimates used in the modified <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> argument below.</p>
</div>
</section>